,"type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"Interaction_DragView","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_DragView"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_DragView"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Drags a layer in any direction with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"text":" patch, which wires its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"output ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card snaps back to its resting position.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/toolbar(id:content:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/toolbar(id:content:)","title":"toolbar(id:content:)","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"toolbar","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","ki